Z||000002||SLAMMED87GT||11-18-2001||11:52 AM||||Hey Cali- That's cool. Around here it's not quite the same attitude. (I sense a lot of jealousy!) For example at a show hosted by a Corvette club in the Twin Cities area, I think maybe 2 came by to talk to me and the other guy that brought his Fiero. ALthough the Corvette guys didn't really check out any other cars besides there own! <P>I have met some nice guys with vettes, some that I have even persuaded to buy a Fiero!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFieroSig.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto540 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||1
Z||000003||3.8T Fiero GT||11-18-2001||12:34 PM||||ddddddddaaaaaaaammmmmnnnnnnnnnn<P>------------------<BR>*Your ASS here*   <IMG SRC="http://www.plaudersmilies.de/rough/zzwhip.gif"> <BR><B>"A 3.8T makes and excellent "RICE" cooker"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||California Kid||11-18-2001||12:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by VeeSixGeeTee:<BR><B>Sweet!, haha...I think I would have felt kinda left out, but maybe not?  So did most of them like your sweet ride?  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>When I pulled in only 4 had arrived, I asked if I could join they're group as I had read about their get together off their web site. They responded "No Problem, park it", think some interest was sparked when I came rumbling in (if you haven't heard the sound clip of my car, go to post by "artherd" topic California Kid can't go 55).<P>These four guy's looked over the engine compartment with serious interest. Now notice where everyone else parked when they showed up (see photo). Typically I find that most Vette owners don't get real interested in my car until they hear it's got a V8 and putting out more horse than theirs. Word did get around the group, I did open the hatch for quite a few of them, and answered a lot of questions. Another thing I notice about most Vette people is that they don't modify their cars, just add seat covers, nice floor mats, so on......these are the guy's that won't come near your Fiero.<P>Think my little car pretty much freaked them out, did get some very nice compliments.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||California Kid||11-18-2001||04:00 PM||||Checked the Corvette Forum and they did post pictures of my car!<BR> <A HREF="http://forums.corvetteforum.com/zerothread?id=185388" TARGET=_blank>http://forums.corvetteforum.com/zerothread?id=185388</A> <P>They had a "Corvette Shoot Out" at Lapeer Dragway the following day. For Pics and results of their times go to: <A HREF="http://forums.corvetteforum.com/zerothread?id=184920" TARGET=_blank>http://forums.corvetteforum.com/zerothread?id=184920</A> <P>Times weren't great, but I know that track doesn't "hook" for sh$$ when it's cool.||||reg||1
